# npm audit policy: fail on critical only (audit-level applies to the exit code,
# not to what `npm audit` reports). Re-check on every dependency upgrade, and set
# this to "moderate" or "low" once the findings below clear.
#
# Two root causes remain (22 findings: 18 moderate, 4 low, none high or critical),
# neither fixable by upgrading as of aws-cdk-lib 2.275.0 and jest 29:
#
# - GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249: minimatch <11.0.1 DoS through glob pattern amplification.
#   * The copy bundled inside aws-cdk-lib (10.2.6) cannot be replaced with
#     package.json overrides, because npm overrides do not apply to bundled
#     dependencies (tested, including a scoped "aws-cdk-lib" override). CDK uses it
#     at synth time on our own repository paths, not on untrusted patterns.
#   * The copies under jest's glob and test-exclude (3.x) cannot be lifted either.
#     A global "minimatch" override to 11.x installs, but breaks `npm run
#     test:coverage` ("minimatch is not a function"): test-exclude 6 calls
#     minimatch as a function and 11.x only exports { minimatch }. Moving to jest 30
#     does not help, its dependency chain uses minimatch 9.x and 10.x, both still
#     below 11.0.1. Do not reintroduce that override without running test:coverage.
#   Clears when aws-cdk-lib and the jest toolchain move to minimatch >=11.0.1.
#
# - GHSA-gcqx-w48m-w2h4: deepmerge <=4.3.1 prototype poisoning in mergeObject().
#   No patched release exists (4.3.1 is the latest). Dev-only: jest-config uses it
#   to merge its own configuration. The jest, ts-jest and @jest/* entries in the
#   audit output are flagged only because they depend on it.
#
# Do not run "npm audit fix --force": for these it proposes downgrading jest to 25.
audit-level=critical
